- content_for :title, "Content scorecard"
- th_class = "px-3 py-2 font-medium whitespace-nowrap"
- potential = @sort.key == "potential"
- compared = !@scorecard.previous.nil?
- tab = "rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium"
-# Top and bottom quarters coloured, so where an entry is strong or weak
-# reads along its row without comparing figures.
- rank_class = ->(rank) { if rank.nil? then "text-slate-400" elsif rank >= 0.75 then "text-emerald-700" elsif rank < 0.25 then "text-amber-700" else "text-slate-700" end }

%div{class: "mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3"}
  %div
    %h1{class: "text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight"} Content scorecard
    %p{class: "mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500"}
      Every entry ranked on each measure there is of it: how much it's read and liked, how it does in search, how far readers get,
      and how fast it loads.
  = link_to list_url(@period, @filtering, @sort, format: :csv),
    class: "inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-50" do
    = icon("download", size: 14)
    Export CSV

= render "shared/stats_filters", stats: @stats, period: @period, filtering: @filtering, keep: [@sort], likes_note: false

%nav{class: "mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-1", aria: {label: "Order"}}
  - ContentScorecard::SORTS.each do |key, label|
    - current = key == @sort.key
    = link_to label, list_url(@period, @filtering, ContentScorecardReportsController::Sort.new(key)),
      class: [tab, current ? "bg-slate-900 text-white" : "text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100 hover:text-slate-900"], aria: {current: (current ? "true" : nil)}

- if @rows.empty?
  = render "shared/empty_state", message: "No feed entries yet. Sync them from Feed entries."
- else
  %p{class: "mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600"}
    - if potential
      Seen most in search yet weakest overall first: how often Google shows an entry, times how far its score falls short.
    - else
      Strongest across every measure first. The score is the average of an entry's place on each measure, 100% being top on all
      of them; a measure it has no figure for counts as middling.
  %div{class: "relative overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm"}
    %table{class: "w-full border-collapse text-sm"}
      %thead{class: "border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 text-slate-600"}
        %tr
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right", aria: {label: "Row number"}} #
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-left"} Entry
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} w-40 text-left"}= potential ? "Potential" : "Score"
          - ContentScorecard::MEASURES.each do |measure|
            %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right"}= measure.label
          - if @ai.covered
            %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right", title: "Google's total for #{l(@ai.covered.begin)} – #{l(@ai.covered.end)}, from the latest Generative AI upload; shown, not ranked"} AI impressions
      %tbody
        - @rows.each_with_index do |row, index|
          - figure = potential ? row.potential : row.score
          - earlier = @scorecard.previous_row(row)
          %tr{class: "border-t border-slate-100"}
            %td{class: "px-3 py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-slate-400"}= index + 1
            %td{class: "w-full px-3 py-2"}
              = blog_page_link(row.item.entry.name, page_view_path(row.item.path, **@period.query), live: row.item.path)
              %span{class: "text-xs text-slate-500"} #{row.item.type.capitalize} · #{l(row.item.entry.published_at.to_date)}
            %td{class: "px-3 py-2"}
              - if figure
                %div{class: "flex items-center gap-2"}
                  %div{class: "flex-1"}= meter(figure * 100, 100, label: "#{potential ? "Potential" : "Score"} of #{row.item.entry.name}")
                  %span{class: "w-10 shrink-0 text-right tabular-nums"}
                    = number_to_percentage(figure * 100, precision: 0)
                    - before_figure = (potential ? earlier&.potential : earlier&.score) if compared
                    = row_change(figure, before_figure, CompareHelper::HIGHER_RATE_IS_BETTER) if before_figure
              - else
                %span{class: "text-slate-400"} —
            - ContentScorecard::MEASURES.each do |measure|
              - value = row.values[measure.key]
              %td{class: "px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums #{rank_class.(row.ranks[measure.key])}",
                title: (row.ranks[measure.key] && "Ahead of #{number_to_percentage(row.ranks[measure.key] * 100, precision: 0)} of entries")}
                - if value.nil?
                  \—
                - elsif measure.key == :performance
                  = (value * 100).round
                - else
                  = metric_value(value, measure.format)
                -# Speed is Lighthouse's latest score, not the period's, so there's no earlier one to compare.
                - before_value = earlier&.values&.[](measure.key) if compared && measure.key != :performance
                = row_change(value, before_value, CompareHelper::Measure.new(false, measure.format)) if value && before_value
            - if @ai.covered
              %td{class: "px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums text-slate-700"}= number_with_delimiter(@scorecard.ai_impressions(row))
  %p{class: "mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500"}
    Green is an entry's top quarter on a measure and amber its bottom. Likes per view needs #{BlogStats::MIN_VIEWS_FOR_RATE}+ views and
    CTR #{Google::SearchConsole::Summary::MIN_IMPRESSIONS}+ impressions; time engaged and read-through need
    #{Google::Analytics::Insights::MIN_VIEWS}+ Analytics views. Speed is Lighthouse's phone score. Search and Analytics cover every country.
    - if @ai.covered
      AI impressions are Google's totals for #{l(@ai.covered.begin)} – #{l(@ai.covered.end)} from the latest Generative AI upload, whatever
      period is picked, so they're shown but don't count toward the score.
